Yes, there is a way to have larger tiles: you start
by acquiring or making some larger tiles, then you
tell the game where they are, and how big they are,
in the "plain text" runtime startup file (.nethackrc
in some operating systems, defaults.nh in others).

If you go to the nethack.org site, you'll find, at least
in the MS-Windows download page, toward the bottom, a
double sized (32x32 pixels) tile set available to
download and a set of instructions for how to modify
the defaults.nh file to use it.

Elsewhere, you can find tile sets up to 128x128
(the "absurd tile set"), and some "non-square" tiles
better fit to real world screen shapes (Goeduck's
tile set).

I don't know how much storage your smartphone has,
but (uncompressed) tile image files get huge
rapidly. Also, not all tile sizes "work" in existing
NetHack executables.

I do know that the MS-Windows executable binaries
run into trouble with tile sizes somewhere larger
than 56x56 (which works for me, while 64x64 does
not), no matter how much RAM the computer running
the game may contain. Probably this is an indexing
problem in the compiler used, rather than any real
"NetHack" limitation [but it might also be a limit
in the device video display real estate for "off
screen" parts of images, or some such].

The point of this sidetrack is just to warn you that
you might not succeed in getting tiles "as big as
you want", or making them work, but can probably
improve on what you have now.

